specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:8:Every tool registered in `src/orchestration/tools/registry.ts` declares a JSON Schema `inputSchema` that is forwarded to the configured AI provider, and `ToolRegistry.execute` validates the model-supplied `input` against that schema before calling the tool's executor. When validation fails, `execute` returns a rejection `ToolResponse` describing what was wrong rather than throwing, so the orchestrator feeds the failure back to the model as a `tool_result` within the existing tool-round budget.
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:12:- When `input` omits a property listed in `required`, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the missing property as required, including its parent path when nested, and never invokes the executor. ([validated by: rejects input missing a required property with a ToolResponse and never calls the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L16), [validated by: returns a rejection for a missing required property without calling the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L6), [validated by: includes the complete parent path when a nested required property is missing](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L91))
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:13:- When `input` supplies a property whose value does not match its declared JSON Schema type, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` naming the failing field path and expected type without invoking the executor, and neither `result` nor the emitted log record contains the offending property value. ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed property naming the field and expected type without leaking the offending value to the result or logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L46), [validated by: names the property path and expected type for a wrong-typed value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L23))
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:14:- When `input` satisfies `required`, declared property types and `enum`, `ToolRegistry.execute` invokes the executor once and passes the input object through unchanged — including undeclared extra properties — without injecting `additionalProperties: false`, coercing types or applying defaults. ([validated by: passes a valid input and undeclared properties through unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L47))
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:15:- When `ToolRegistry.execute` is called with a tool name that has not been registered, it throws `Unknown tool: <name>` because an unregistered tool is a programming or configuration error rather than a recoverable input mistake. ([validated by: throws for an unregistered tool name](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L64))
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:19:- A static schema that cannot be compiled makes registration fail synchronously and names the tool. ([validated by: rejects an invalid static schema during registration](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.registration.test.ts#L4))
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:20:- A static `ToolDefinition` has its `inputSchema` compiled once at `register` time, so a schema that is not valid JSON Schema throws synchronously from `register` with an error message naming the offending tool ([validated by: throws at register time naming the tool when a static inputSchema cannot be compiled](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L94)).
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:21:- A static tool's `inputSchema` is compiled at `register` time and reused on every `execute` call without re-reading or re-compiling `definition.inputSchema`. ([validated by: compiles a static schema once across repeated executions](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L117))
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:22:- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves its definition on each `execute` call and validates against the `inputSchema` returned for that call, caching compiled validators by schema object reference (`WeakMap`) so distinct returned schemas each enforce their own rules. ([validated by: resolves and validates a function-valued tool definition on each call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L70))
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:24:## Orchestrator tool-loop recovery
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:26:- Because a schema rejection returns a `ToolResponse` instead of throwing, `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` sends the rejection `result` back to the provider as a `tool_result` message, allowing the model to issue a corrected tool call on the next round and complete the turn within `maxToolRounds` ([validated by: returns a schema rejection as a tool_result in the orchestrator loop so the model can correct the call on the next round](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L112), [validated by: returns a schema rejection as a tool_result so the provider can retry](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L401)).
specs/hal-engine-config-hooks/spec.md:12:- A hook passed through `orchestrator.hooks` is forwarded to the orchestrator and fires ([validated by: forwards an orchestrator hook, so one passed through the config actually fires](../../src/config.test.ts#L17)).
specs/hal-engine-config-hooks/spec.md:13:- An engine built with no `orchestrator` key at all still processes a message, so the field is optional in fact and not only in the type ([validated by: processes a message when the config declares no orchestrator key at all](../../src/config.test.ts#L93)).
specs/hal-engine-config-hooks/spec.md:14:- A `beforeModelResponse` hook installed through config is handed the base system prompt built from `prompt`, proving the hook reaches the orchestrator and is wired into the prompt pipeline rather than only being stored on the config ([validated by: hands a config-installed beforeModelResponse hook the built base system prompt, not merely storing it](../../src/config.test.ts#L106)).
specs/hal-engine-config-hooks/spec.md:15:- The value the hook returns then replaces the system prompt the provider receives; this is exercised at the orchestrator layer because `HalEngineConfig.provider` takes a `ProviderConfig` and offers no seam to inject a recording provider through config ([validated by: replaces system prompt with returned value](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L194)).
specs/hal-engine-config-hooks/spec.md:16:- For a session that completes without error the hooks fire in the order `beforeSession` → `beforeUserInput` → `afterUserInput` → `beforeModelResponse` → `afterModelResponse` → `afterSession` ([validated by: fires the lifecycle hooks in documented order for a session that completes without error](../../src/config.test.ts#L130)).
specs/hal-engine-config-hooks/spec.md:20:- The engine's `start()` method rejects the returned promise when it cannot bind the configured port, rather than emitting an unhandled error event that would take the process down ([validated by: rejects instead of taking the process down with an unhandled error event](../../src/config.test.ts#L172)).
specs/hal-engine-providers/spec.md:101:Supports streaming through `sendMessage` and structured JSON output through `generateStructured` ([validated by: streams text chunks from Vertex AI response](../../src/providers/vertex/vertexProvider.test.ts#L55), [structured](../../src/providers/vertex/vertexProvider.test.ts#L208)).
specs/hal-engine-providers/spec.md:157:- A function call part becomes a `tool_use` chunk. Vertex reports no call id of its own, so the function's name is used as the id as well ([validated by: yields tool_use chunks for function calls](../../src/providers/vertex/vertexProvider.test.ts#L76)).
specs/hal-engine-providers/spec.md:158:- A `MAX_TOKENS` finish reason becomes the stop reason `max_tokens`, so a truncated reply is distinguishable from a completed one ([validated by: maps MAX_TOKENS finish reason](../../src/providers/vertex/vertexProvider.test.ts#L110)).
specs/hal-engine-providers/spec.md:159:- A candidate carrying no parts is skipped rather than emitted as an empty chunk ([validated by: skips chunks with no candidate parts](../../src/providers/vertex/vertexProvider.test.ts#L158)).
specs/hal-engine-providers/spec.md:160:- The `assistant` role is sent to Vertex as `model`, which is the only role name its API accepts for a prior reply; `user` passes through unchanged ([validated by: maps assistant role to model for Vertex API](../../src/providers/vertex/vertexProvider.test.ts#L175)).
specs/hal-engine-providers/spec.md:164:- `generateStructured` sets `responseMimeType` to `application/json` and passes the schema with its type names upper-cased, which is the form the Vertex SDK expects ([validated by: configures model with responseMimeType and responseSchema](../../src/providers/vertex/vertexProvider.test.ts#L228)).
specs/hal-engine-providers/spec.md:165:- A response body that is not valid JSON raises `AIError` with code `PARSE_ERROR`, rather than returning something the caller would have to re-check ([validated by: throws AIError with PARSE_ERROR on invalid JSON](../../src/providers/vertex/vertexProvider.test.ts#L263)).
specs/hal-engine-providers/spec.md:169:- A message naming `429` or `RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED` becomes `RATE_LIMITED` and is marked retryable ([validated by: throws AIError with RATE_LIMITED on 429](../../src/providers/vertex/vertexProvider.test.ts#L122)).
specs/hal-engine-providers/spec.md:170:- A message naming `401`, `403` or `PERMISSION_DENIED` becomes `AUTH_ERROR` ([validated by: throws AIError with AUTH_ERROR on permission denied](../../src/providers/vertex/vertexProvider.test.ts#L134)).
specs/hal-engine-providers/spec.md:171:- Anything the mapping cannot classify becomes `PROVIDER_ERROR`, so an SDK error never reaches the caller as a raw `Error` ([validated by: falls back to PROVIDER_ERROR for a failure it cannot classify](../../src/providers/vertex/vertexProvider.test.ts#L146)).
specs/hal-engine-providers/spec.md:172:- The mapping is shared: a failure raised during `generateStructured` is classified exactly as the same failure during `sendMessage` would be ([validated by: throws mapped AIError on Vertex API failure](../../src/providers/vertex/vertexProvider.test.ts#L277)).
specs/hal-engine-providers/spec.md:232:- `sendMessage` streams `Mock response to: "<last user message>"` one word at a time ([validated by: streams word-by-word response echoing user input](../../src/providers/mock/mockProvider.test.ts#L7)).
